.vercel
node_modules/

# Local env files — never commit secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Physician data never belongs in this repository ────────────────────────
# This repo is PUBLIC. Roster/submission data lives in Supabase; the tables
# there are the source of truth (see SUPABASE_TABLES.md).
#
# This used to name a single file (sender-physician-match.csv). A denylist of
# one filename does not generalise: csv_2569_01-04/ was added later and walked
# straight past it, publishing 773 rows of name + department + score. So the
# rule is now shape-based — ignore ALL csv/xlsx by default and opt individual
# files back in only when they are demonstrably not personal data.
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls

# Opt-ins go here, e.g.:
#   !test/fixtures/synthetic-roster.csv
# .github/workflows/pii-guard.yml also fails any PR that adds a file whose
# header looks like personal data, so an opt-in still has to be a real one.
